      "content": "Your MSA should include a clear pricing clause that either caps price increases to a reasonable percentage annually or ties them to a transparent market index, preventing arbitrary hikes. To address supply chain risks, you'll also need a specific force majeure section and meaningful volume guarantee provisions that hold the supplier accountable if they cannot meet your committed orders. Finally, ensure robust termination rights and deep credit clauses to protect your business relationships and financial stability if the supplier encounters significant volatility.",
