    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. On the pricing side, how do I handle things if a supplier tries to hide extra costs in the fine print or uses \"unforeseen circumstances\" to bypass the cap we agreed on? I'm really trying to make sure we aren't blindsided by bad faith tactics or hidden fee structures.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To prevent hidden costs, your MSA must explicitly define what constitutes the \"base price\" and include a mandatory audit clause that allows you to verify any additional charges before they are finalized. Regarding \"unforeseen circumstances,\" you should define a narrow, objective list of valid Force Majeure events and require the supplier to provide third-party proof before any price adjustment can be justified, ensuring they cannot use vague excuses to bypass your caps. Additionally, including a \"good faith negotiation\" provision will obligate both parties to communicate openly and in writing if ambiguity arises during the supplier's claims process.",
      "source": "target",
